```javascript
var n = processed.select('B8').count().rename('n_clear');
Map.addLayer(n, {min: 0, max: 30, palette: ['red', 'yellow', 'green']}, 'Clear observations');
Map.addLayer(n.lt(10).selfMask(), {palette: ['red']}, 'Fewer than 10');
```
Coastal pixels and the windward slopes of hills usually have the fewest clear looks. A classification there rests on a few dates, possibly all from one season, so its median is less stable and class confidence lower. Report the count map with the classification, or mask areas below a threshold you can defend.

